    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "Compound of 静 (shizu, bound morpheme indicating “quietness” or “calmness”) + か (-ka, suffixing element used to form na adjectives). The shizu portion is cognate with the shizu in 静まる (shizumaru, “to become quiet”) and 沈む (shizumu, “to sink; to set (such as the sun or moon); to become depressed”). This shizu might also be related to 下 (shita, “down; below”)."
      },
      {
        "quote": "First attested in the Nihon Shoki of 720 CE."
      }
    ],
